  "action_summary": "Replaces the next layer of the menu with a closure RULE. Measured first, and it corrects round 22: on round 23 searched organs the concept bridge DOES fire (1,2,3 concepts after periods 3,5,7), so round 22's zero-concepts diagnosis was a symptom round 23 removed. But the library is INERT: T(x)+x and T(x)*x are refused cold and refused warm, with or without three learned tables, and the compounding test is flat at 2 questions cold and warm because 2 is the information floor, so cost can no longer measure learning. The fix is one closure rule: invert a combining operation and solve for the table's block in the residual, depth 1 over a small basis. Cold with writers disabled, T(x)+x, T(x)-x, T(x)*x and T(x)+x*x are each expressed at 37/37 held-out in 3 questions, all four refused before. 15 adversarial cases produce zero false claims. The candidate count is bounded and does not grow with period. Also records that x*x is now correctly solved rather than refused, which overturned a round-23 assertion of mine.",
